{"toolCallId":"call_e09d91e867b44a8eab3233a6a85d2531","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n---\n\n## RELATED DOCUMENTS\n\n- **Implementation Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Task Breakdown**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Verification Checklist**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Decision Records**: See ADR-001 in `plan.md`; this packet keeps no separate `decision-record.md`\n\n---\n\n=== plan tail ===\n- Bare integer output (`0`): it is marginally easier to consume but drops the level name and gives a caller no stable prefix to anchor on.\n- `--quiet` wins over `--json`: silent precedence produces a text line for a caller that asked for JSON, which is the failure mode hardest to notice.\n- A new `--format level` option: a larger surface for the same one-line result, and it would invite a second format later.\n\n---\n\n=== tasks tail ===\n## L3+: Documentation Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All spec documents are synchronized. Check: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh $P --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P1] The help text and the header block agree on the flag's contract. Check: both name \"only the recommended-level line\" as the behavior.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/223-deepseek-final","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"c14cc7","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
